Q: NeoForge: Couldn&#39;t parse item model A: <p>The file <code>bottle_of_air.json</code> you currently have is the <em>raw</em> model and should be placed in <code>/assets/chemistrycraft/models/item</code>. The directory <code>/assets/chemistrycraft/items</code> is for the <em>processor files</em> that Minecraft now uses to select which raw model to use for an item.</p>
<p>The solution here is not just changing the location of the raw model, the file <code>/assets/chemistrycraft/items/bottle_of_air.json</code> must look differently; in your case, like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;model&quot;: {
    &quot;type&quot;: &quot;minecraft:model&quot;, 
    &quot;model&quot;: &quot;chemistrycraft:item/bottle_of_air&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>&quot;minecraft:model&quot;</code> type means &quot;use a static raw model&quot;, and the <code>&quot;model&quot;</code> key is referencing your raw model at <code>/assets/chemistrycraft/models/item/bottle_of_air.json</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;parent&quot;: &quot;minecraft:item/generated&quot;,
  &quot;textures&quot;: {
    &quot;layer0&quot;: &quot;chemistrycraft:item/bottle_of_air&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>See <a href="https://minecraft.wiki/w/Items_model_definition" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this wiki page</a> for more info on how to define models in <code>/assets/&lt;mod_id&gt;/items</code>.</p>
